{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-08-21T07:06:42.645050+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-21T08:11:55.649785+00:00", "id": 22040878, "conceptrecid": "22040877", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22040878", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22040877", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22040878", "metadata": {"title": "Analysis and assessment of the regional impacts of online platforms", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22040878", "publication_date": "2025-03-28", "description": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Despite the global nature of e-commerce, retail markets remain inherently local systems. Consequently, the nationwide expansion of online platforms generates heterogeneous effects on local economies.<em> </em>This paper evaluates the impact of major marketplaces (Ozon and Wildberries) on the competitive environment and trading activity within Russian municipalities. </span><span>A key methodological feature of the study is the use of the number of pickup points (PUPs; per 1000 residents) as a proxy metric for platform penetration. Based on panel data from over 1400 municipalities we establish a positive relationship between PUPs and traditional retail outlets availability (number per 1000 of residents), suggesting a complementarity between online and offline retail formats. The positive short-term effect of pickup point network expansion on per capita retail turnover suggests that online platforms stimulate local consumption. </span><span>The application of the Instrumental Variables (IV) approach to control for endogeneity allows interpreting the obtained estimates not merely as <span>correlational</span>, but as causal effects of local market transformation.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Antonenko, Natalia", "affiliation": "Gaidar Institute for Economic Policy"}, {"name": "Savina, Alexandra", "affiliation": "Gaidar Institute for Economic Policy"}, {"name": "Ponomarev, Yuriy", "affiliation": "Gaidar Institute for Economic Policy"}], "keywords": ["Territorial effects, online platform; marketplaces logistics infrastructure; fixed effects panel regression; endogeneity; instrumental variables; shift-share"], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22040877"}}]}}, "title": "Analysis and assessment of the regional impacts of online platforms", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22040878", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22040878?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22040878", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22040878", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22040878", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040877", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22040877", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22040877", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22040877", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22040878/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22040878/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22040878/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22040878/access/request"